<!--
  Chapter 59 — Cloud-Native on AWS, Azure & GCP.
    identity/    TokenVerifier (RS256 JWTs checked offline against an issuer's JWKS: what a cloud token service does)
                 and TrustPolicy (a role trusting one audience and named service accounts)
    retry/       the AWS SDK v2 retry modes (none, legacy, standard, adaptive) with RetryQuota and ClientRateLimiter
    serverless/  FunctionPool (a day of requests replayed against keep-warm instances), Traffic, CostModel
    resources/   k8s/workload-identity.yaml (a service account and a pod with a projected token for the cloud)
  verify/run.sh exchanges real k3s service-account tokens, runs SDK-style clients against a throttled API, and
  measures a JVM cold start for the functions-or-containers model.
-->
